        "original_id": "b527590e-bb44-57a1-83f2-29e10a77db17",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ben Elton, Andrew Lloyd Webber, Glenn Slater, Frederick Forsyth, Summer Strallen\n- Works: The Young Ones, Blackadder, We Will Rock You, Love Never Dies, The Phantom of the Opera, The Sound of Music, Hollyoaks\n- Topics: Alternative comedy, West End theatre, musicals, television\n\nFacts:\n- Ben Elton was born on 3 May 1959 and is an English comedian, author, playwright, actor, and director.\n- In the 1980s, Ben Elton was part of London's alternative comedy movement.\n- In the 1980s, Ben Elton became a writer on The Young Ones and Blackadder while continuing as a stand-up comedian on stage and television.\n- In 2002, Ben Elton wrote the musical We Will Rock You.\n- In 2010, Ben Elton wrote Love Never Dies, a sequel to The Phantom of the Opera.\n- Love Never Dies is a romantic musical with music by Andrew Lloyd Webber, lyrics by Glenn Slater, and a book by Andrew Lloyd Webber, Ben Elton, Frederick Forsyth, and Glenn Slater.\n- Ben Elton has published 15 novels.\n- Summer Strallen played Meg Giry in the West End production of Love Never Dies.\n- Summer Strallen also played Maria von Trapp in Andrew Lloyd Webber's revival of The Sound of Music at the London Palladium.\n- Summer Strallen played the fictional character Summer Shaw in the British Channel 4 soap opera Hollyoaks.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "542f2281-c272-5ee9-a7d9-5eddc8a5ba52",
        "text": "Page: Ben Elton. Sentence: Benjamin Charles Elton (born 3 May 1959) is an English comedian, author, playwright, actor and director.\nPage: Ben Elton. Sentence: He was a part of London's alternative comedy movement of the 1980s and became a writer on series such as \"The Young Ones\" and \"Blackadder\", as well as continuing as a stand-up comedian on stage and television.\nPage: Ben Elton. Sentence: Since then he has published 15 novels and written the musicals \"We Will Rock You\" (2002) and \"Love Never Dies\" (2010), the sequel to \"The Phantom of the Opera\".\nPage: Love Never Dies (musical). Sentence: Love Never Dies is a romantic musical composed by Andrew Lloyd Webber with lyrics by Glenn Slater and a book by Lloyd Webber, Ben Elton, Frederick Forsyth and Slater.\nPage: Summer Strallen. Sentence: Her most notable theatre credits include Meg Giry in the West End production of \"Love Never Dies\" and Maria von Trapp in Andrew Lloyd Webber's revival of \"The Sound of Music\" at the London Palladium.\nPage: Summer Shaw. Sentence: Summer Shaw is a fictional character from the British Channel 4 soap opera, \"Hollyoaks\", played by Summer Strallen.",
